bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_typed_optional_holding_user_none_takes_some_arm_2026-11-27, 0, "Repro (seeds aa542919a298e130 base and b45d80cfb2580c23, aarch64; found while fixing seed_jit_any_match_bare_none_arm_misses_user_enum_none_2026-11-27, not changed by it): enum Q: None | Here(i64); fn u(x: Q?) -> i64: match x: Some(v): return 1 / None: return 0; val a: Q? = Q.None; u(a) is 0 on the interpreter (its bare None pattern matches any enum value whose variant is named None, so the present Q.None takes the None arm) and 1 on the JIT (typed optional: present, Some arm). if x.?: agrees on both (1). The two engines disagree on whether a typed Q? holding Q.None is present under Some/None arms; which one is the intended language rule needs an owner decision before either side changes."

